  "worked_solution": "For any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,z) & =\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8x,\\,12{x}^{2},\\,z\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $12{x}^{2}.$",
